=== RUN   TestHostRejectsHostPortMistake
helixendpoint: WARNING: HELIX_AGENT_HOST="agent.internal:7061" is not a usable URL host, so the placeholder host "localhost" is used instead. This variable takes a BARE host — no scheme, path, query, fragment, userinfo or port. A colon is accepted only inside a genuine IPv6 literal, so a "host:port" value is rejected rather than re-interpreted, and a value carrying "/", "?", "#" or "@" is rejected for the same reason: appending the port after one of those puts it in the wrong URL component and the address silently points elsewhere. Use HELIX_AGENT_BASE_URL to inject host and port as one string.
helixendpoint: WARNING: HELIX_AGENT_HOST="example.com:80" is not a usable URL host, so the placeholder host "localhost" is used instead. This variable takes a BARE host — no scheme, path, query, fragment, userinfo or port. A colon is accepted only inside a genuine IPv6 literal, so a "host:port" value is rejected rather than re-interpreted, and a value carrying "/", "?", "#" or "@" is rejected for the same reason: appending the port after one of those puts it in the wrong URL component and the address silently points elsewhere. Use HELIX_AGENT_BASE_URL to inject host and port as one string.
helixendpoint: WARNING: HELIX_AGENT_HOST=<value withheld: may carry credentials> is not a usable URL host, so the placeholder host "localhost" is used instead. This variable takes a BARE host — no scheme, path, query, fragment, userinfo or port. A colon is accepted only inside a genuine IPv6 literal, so a "host:port" value is rejected rather than re-interpreted, and a value carrying "/", "?", "#" or "@" is rejected for the same reason: appending the port after one of those puts it in the wrong URL component and the address silently points elsewhere. Use HELIX_AGENT_BASE_URL to inject host and port as one string.
